    "body": "> I went through the spec and I think the closest equivalent to what we do in chrome is to extend the condition and call [URL and history update steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#url-and-history-update-steps) also for reloads. I don't understand what makes this \"not appropriate\".\n\nI think that may be the correct solution, but I think the [URL and history update steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#url-and-history-update-steps)  are currently not resilient to   `historyHandling` being set to `\"reload\"`.  In particular, I'm not sure [Finalize a same-document navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#finalize-a-same-document-navigation) should be called in the `\"reload\"` case.",
